{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall place the cover, etc. And into the ark you shall put, etc.</b> It is difficult: why was it necessary to say a second time <b>and into the ark you shall put</b>, after it already said above ״וְנָתַתָּ אֶת הָעֵדוּת״ etc.? And Rashi, his memory for a blessing, explains that it intends to say that he should first place the Testimony and afterward place the cover upon it — this far. It is implied from his words that there was room to err and think that he should place the Testimony upon the ark, and my mind is not comfortable saying there is room for such an error — all the more so since there is no place there, for it is the place of the cherubim. And furthermore, he should have said in the first verse, instead of the word ״אֶל״ — ״תּוֹךְ״, and then he would not have needed to write a second time ״וְאֶל הָאָרֹן״. And there is yet more to ask on this. And Rabbi Elijah Mizrachi, his memory for a blessing, wrote on this things that are not up to the height of his wisdom. And I saw that he wished to support the words of Rashi from the words of Ibn Ezra, and with apology for his honor — the words of Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra are that he comes to correct the meaning, so that it should not be difficult for you in the verse that it placed the giving of the cover before the giving of the Testimony, when it would be proper to give the Testimony first; therefore he said ״וּכְבָר״ etc. — not to explain that the entire verse comes to say that he should not place the Testimony above the cover, for this on the contrary is already understood from the first verse, and the error on the contrary [would arise] from the second verse." "And the correct interpretation in my eyes is to say that the intent of the verse is to include in it an act of placing, to say that after he places the cover upon the ark, they shall never leave it for all generations — like the rule of a Torah scroll, which He commanded to set to the side, etc. And they said, their memory for a blessing (Deuteronomy Rabbah 9:9), that its rule is that if there is a discrepancy between tribe and tribe in their scrolls — for every tribe wrote one Torah scroll — they verify the scroll from the scroll deposited in the House of YHWH, and He said that the Testimony is there so that they shall never leave. And therefore it multiplied placing after placing, and for this reason we also understand why it placed the giving of the cover before the giving of the Testimony, for it comes only to say that after they are placed in the ark and covered with the cover, they are placed placed there forever — and understand." "It further intends: that he shall not place the Testimony in the ark until the ark is complete with its cover, and not before. And this is what it says — <b>and you shall place the cover</b> etc., then <b>into the ark you shall put the Testimony</b>." "It is also possible to say according to their words, their memory for a blessing (Bava Batra 14b), that the tablets and the fragments of the tablets are placed in the ark; therefore it said it twice — once corresponding to the whole tablets and the second corresponding to the broken ones." "And by way of remez it appears: that it comes to hint to him that even though the cover is above the Testimony — for they are inside the ark below the cover — they are in the aspect of being above it. And therefore it arranged the giving of the Testimony after the cover, to say that this is above that — something that would not have been heard thus had it preceded to say ״וְנָתַתָּ אֶת הָעֵדוּת וְגוֹ׳ וְנָתַתָּ אֶת הַכַּפֹּרֶת עַל הָאָרוֹן מִלְמָעְלָה״, which would imply that the cover is merely above the ark [but not above the Testimony in spiritual standing]."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:31.010482097Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}